"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project has received a $2M budget approval and has reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype. The team is expanding with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with an onboarding session set for September 10th. The project is moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, following the completion of the design phase. Strategic partnerships have been established with TechInnovate for AI research. Additionally, the compliance plan budget has been increased to $55,000, and security protocols including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest will be updated starting January next year. The next phase involves user interface enhancements planned for October."
